:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="dolx-changelog">
		<div class="dolx-changelog-hero">
			<span class="dolx-changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.20.12</span></h1>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="dolx-changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Merged with vanilla version 0.5.11.4.
		</li>
		<li>Added the Bailey Expansion
		<ul>
			<li>Integrated Reiyu’s Bailey Expansion.
			</li>
			<li>Fixes and migration support by D.N.A.
			</li>
			<li>Updated the credits and changelog with the appropriate mod-expansion attribution.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added sensitivity medication and expanded sensitivity mechanics
		<ul>
			<li>The hospital pharmacy now sells 14-packs of sensitivity suppressants and stimulants.
			</li>
			<li>Each dose lasts 16 hours and is limited to one dose per day.
			</li>
			<li>Taking one medication replaces the opposing effect.
			</li>
			<li>Suppressants reduce effective sensitivity to 0.25.
			</li>
			<li>Stimulants add 3 effective sensitivity, allowing normally sensitive characters to experience high-sensitivity effects.
			</li>
			<li>Passive nipple rubbing is now prevented by pasties, tape, binders, form-fitting leotards, and swim shirts.
			</li>
			<li>Genital rubbing no longer occurs with skirt-only outfits, one-piece bottoms, or boxers worn by vagina-only characters.
			</li>
			<li>Trousers and boxers containing a penis can still cause rubbing.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added a post-encounter summary
		<ul>
			<li>Added a new <strong>Show post-encounter summary</strong> toggle under <strong>Settings &gt; Enemy Stats Display</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>The summary records how many times the player and other participants orgasmed.
			</li>
			<li>It also records where cum was received or given, along with clothing that was destroyed or stolen.
			</li>
			<li>Supports human, beast, tentacle, and swarm encounters.
			</li>
			<li>Dream encounters are excluded.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added a new alternative-spriteset in option
		<ul>
			<li>Players can now always use the alternative spriteset where one is available, regardless of their current body.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Expanded the Random game mode setting
		<ul>
			<li>Random game mode now recursively randomizes all registered toggles, sliders, and choices.
			</li>
			<li>This currently covers 446 settings across X-Change, combat, AMC, economy and inflation, rebalancing, fetishes, identity, UI options, and more.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added a <strong>Resist heat with willpower</strong> setting
		<ul>
			<li>When enabled, characters with enough willpower can resist losing control during heat, matching the previous behaviour.
			</li>
			<li>When disabled, heat ignores willpower checks and can take control whenever its normal trigger conditions are met.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added a random prison fight event
		<ul>
			<li>The outcome can increase or decrease the player’s prison respect.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Expanded office temp-agency assignments
		<ul>
			<li>Players can now accept assignments while dressed provocatively.
			</li>
			<li>Provocative clothing increases harassment and the chance of dangerous events on the upper floors.
			</li>
			<li>The additional attention also results in larger tips.
			</li>
			<li>Being fully exposed or gagged still prevents the player from accepting an assignment.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Expanded Poppy’s content
		<ul>
			<li>Poppy is now available during realistic childbirth content.
			</li>
			<li>Added additional pregnancy conversations with Poppy.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added Whitney and Robin X-Change reactions.
		</li>
		<li>Added bathroom options for worn insertables
		<ul>
			<li>Players can now scoop out their vagina or anus while wearing a vaginal dildo or butt plug.
			</li>
			<li>The item is temporarily removed, acknowledged with special text, and reinserted afterward.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Improved transformation features
		<ul>
			<li>Players with multiple transformations can now choose which claws are active.
			</li>
			<li>Custom demon colours now display correctly in the mirror.
			</li>
			<li>Claws and long nails now help when escaping Eden’s leash.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Rebalancing</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Updated Insanity and arousal interactions
		<ul>
			<li>Characters with temporary or permanent Insanity no longer notice passive rubbing from underwear or clothing.
			</li>
			<li>Related sensitivity messages and passive arousal gains are prevented.
			</li>
			<li>Insane characters can now sleep or shower even when their arousal would normally be too high.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Buffed the Iron Will trait
		<ul>
			<li>The Fallen Angel Iron Will trait is now retained after using a genome dump.
			</li>
			<li>Iron Will now increases willpower gains by 35%.
			</li>
			<li>Fallen Angels with Iron Will gain 45% more willpower while affected by temporary or permanent Insanity.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Rebalanced advanced combat
		<ul>
			<li>Dodge chance now has diminishing returns above 60%, preventing very high agility from making the player nearly untouchable.
			</li>
			<li>Damage gained from Brawling, Striking, and Kicking now scales more gradually.
			</li>
			<li>Standing Fights now inflict slightly more pain on the player.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed enemy passive dodge not being applied correctly.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed enemy blocking failing to reduce incoming damage because of an incorrect variable name.
			</li>
			<li>Enemy blocking is now capped so that it cannot accidentally heal the enemy.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Extended the Stat Nerf Multiplier
		<ul>
			<li>The Stat Nerf option now affects Combat Extended skills during fights.
			</li>
			<li>Brawling, Striking, Kicking, and Footwork no longer ignore the selected multiplier.
			</li>
			<li>Dodging, strike and kick accuracy, melee and tentacle damage, and stability now scale with the setting.
			</li>
			<li>The character screen now displays the reduction applied to each affected skill.
			</li>
			<li>Skill gains, skill caps, and gym lessons remain unaffected.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added gradual masochism and submission conditioning
		<ul>
			<li>Sustained high pain now has a chance to gradually increase masochism and slightly increase submission.
			</li>
			<li>The chance increases with both pain intensity and duration, up to approximately four hours of continuous pain.
			</li>
			<li>This works alongside existing orgasm and combat-based masochism gains.
			</li>
			<li>The effect is disabled in Soft Mode and during scenes where stat changes are frozen.
			</li>
			<li>Masochism remains capped at the normal maximum of 1,000.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Buffed skilled income sources
		<ul>
			<li>Vanilla version 0.5.11 reduced income from several low and mid-level activities.
			</li>
			<li>Income from affected activities now receives a bonus once the governing skill reaches grade S.
			</li>
			<li>The bonus begins at 10% at grade S and scales up to 50% at grade SSS.
			</li>
			<li>Income remains unchanged below grade S.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Buffed black-market income
		<ul>
			<li>Higher Skulduggery now increases black-market sale values.
			</li>
			<li>The bonus scales up to double value at grade SSS.
			</li>
			<li>Journal estimates now match the actual sale value.
			</li>
			<li>The optional maths-based haggling bonus continues to stack with the Skulduggery bonus.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Rebalanced Ivory Wraith possession resistance
		<ul>
			<li>Adjusted resistance to Ivory Wraith possession.
			</li>
			<li>Rebalanced Bailey love-interest control gains.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Updated shop and spa ban recognition
		<ul>
			<li>X-Change fame below 200 is not recognized, allowing entry.
			</li>
			<li>From 200 to 399 fame, staff are uncertain and still allow entry.
			</li>
			<li>From 400 to 599 fame, staff become suspicious and allow entry while adding a small hidden trespassing increase once per day.
			</li>
			<li>At 600 or more fame, the player is fully recognized and the ban is enforced normally.
			</li>
			<li>Players who are not currently X-Changed continue to be recognized normally.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Fixed X-Change body save and load crashes
		<ul>
			<li>Saving or restoring an X-Change body no longer tries to use a function before it has loaded.
			</li>
			<li>This also fixes crashes during pub spike events and other transformations that automatically save or restore the player’s body.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed runaway pleasure causing repeated orgasms
		<ul>
			<li>Some events could previously increase pleasure far beyond its intended maximum.
			</li>
			<li>The excess could then cause repeated orgasms across later scenes while it slowly drained.
			</li>
			<li>Pleasure gain is now capped slightly above the normal maximum, preserving orgasms during violent encounters without allowing extreme values to accumulate.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed Mickey’s pregnancy-fame recognition
		<ul>
			<li>Pregnancy fame is now recognized when the player is currently pregnant, including during their first pregnancy.
			</li>
			<li>It is also recognized after the player has previously given birth.
			</li>
			<li>Existing pregnancy fame continues to be recognized normally.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed Gwylan’s realistic childbirth content
		<ul>
			<li>Corrected issues affecting Gwylan’s realistic childbirth scene.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed Avery’s Saturday street-date invitation
		<ul>
			<li>The invitation now requires Avery to have been properly introduced.
			</li>
			<li>Completing the science project alone no longer causes Avery to act familiar with the player.
			</li>
			<li>An unknown Avery can now correctly reach the day-20 introduction event.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed redundant Avery NPC generation
		<ul>
			<li>Avery is no longer generated redundantly after the bank-card conversation.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Clarified Robin’s forced X-Change pill scene at the docks
		<ul>
			<li>The scene now clearly states when Robin is forced to take an X-Change pill.
			</li>
			<li>Robin no longer worries about the changed body after the pill’s effects have worn off.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed the heist investigator escape
		<ul>
			<li>The displayed Skulduggery and Athletics labels now match the rolls that are actually performed during investigator chases.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed the bank gala
		<ul>
			<li>Corrected cases where the bank gala could fail to run properly.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed the boutique cash-register theft
		<ul>
			<li>Added the missing continuation link after stealing from the cash register.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed strap-on and dildo underwear checks
		<ul>
			<li>Strap-ons and dildos no longer count as protective underwear.
			</li>
			<li>Genuine underwear protection and clothing-tearing behaviour continue to work normally.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed the Whitney vending-machine event
		<ul>
			<li>Removed a duplicated choice link from the random MMA event.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed a duplicated class-event link
		<ul>
			<li>Class events no longer display the same choice link twice.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed UI issues
		<ul>
			<li>Corrected issues in the money cheat menu for mobile.
			</li>
			<li>Corrected issues affecting <strong>Default Combat Actions</strong> in the attitude menu.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Improved audio performance
		<ul>
			<li>Adjusted audio handling to reduce lag.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed assorted Whitney event typos.
		</li>
	</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
